IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `act-ch19-functions-and-service`

-- Tests for act-ch19-functions-and-service.l4.
-- Every expected value is read from the section named beside the assertion, and was written before the run.

§ `Tests: chapter 19, Parts 19.1, 19.2 and 19.5`

§§ `Part 19.1 and Part 19.2`

-- s 195: law means an Act, subordinate law or disallowable instrument.
#ASSERT `s 195: the kind of document is a law for chapter 19` `an Act`
#ASSERT `s 195: the kind of document is a law for chapter 19` `a subordinate law`
#ASSERT `s 195: the kind of document is a law for chapter 19` `a disallowable instrument`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 195: the kind of document is a law for chapter 19` `a notifiable instrument`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 195: the kind of document is a law for chapter 19` `a commencement notice`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 195: the kind of document is a law for chapter 19` `a statutory instrument of another kind`)

-- s 196 (1): a provision of a law that gives a function to an entity also gives it the powers necessary and convenient to exercise the function.
#ASSERT `s 196 (1): the provision also gives the entity the powers necessary and convenient to exercise the function` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 196 (1): the provision also gives the entity the powers necessary and convenient to exercise the function` FALSE)
-- s 196 (2): the powers are in addition to any other powers of the entity under the law.
#ASSERT `s 196 (2): the powers given under subsection (1) are in addition to any other powers of the entity under the law`
-- s 197: if a law gives a function to an entity, the function may be exercised from time to time.
#ASSERT `s 197: the function may be exercised from time to time` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 197: the function may be exercised from time to time` FALSE)
-- s 199 (1): if a law authorises or requires a body to exercise a function, it may do so by resolution.
#ASSERT `s 199 (1): the body may exercise the function by resolution` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 199 (1): the body may exercise the function by resolution` FALSE)
-- s 199 (2): subsection (1) applies even though a law authorises or requires the function to be exercised in writing.
#ASSERT `s 199 (2): subsection (1) applies to the function` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 199 (2): subsection (1) applies to the function` FALSE
-- s 199 (3): the signature of a person authorised by the body for the purpose is taken to be the signature of the body.
#ASSERT `s 199 (3): the signature of the person authorised by the body is taken to be the signature of the body` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 199 (3): the signature of the person authorised by the body is taken to be the signature of the body` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 199 (3): the signature of the person authorised by the body is taken to be the signature of the body` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 199 (3): the signature of the person authorised by the body is taken to be the signature of the body` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 199 (4): if a law gives a function to a body, the function may be exercised by the body as constituted for the time being.
-- s 199 (4) Example: the ACT Conference Organisers Registration Board's ability to use its power of exemption is not affected by the change of one member.
#ASSERT `s 199 (4): the function may be exercised by the body as constituted for the time being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 199 (4): the function may be exercised by the body as constituted for the time being` FALSE)
-- s 199 (5): the exercise of the function is not affected only because of vacancies in the body's membership.
#ASSERT `s 199 (5): the exercise of the function is affected` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 199 (5): the exercise of the function is affected` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 199 (6): subsections (4) and (5) do not affect any quorum requirement.
-- s 199 (6) Example: the quorum requirement (the chair or deputy chair and 2 other members) still applies at each meeting.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 199 (6): subsections (4) and (5) affect any quorum requirement applying to the body`)
-- s 199 (7): the effect of a thing done by the body does not end only because the membership changes.
#ASSERT `s 199 (7): the effect of the thing done by the body ends` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 199 (7): the effect of the thing done by the body ends` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 199 (8): subsection (7) does not prevent the thing being ended or changed by the body as subsequently constituted.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 199 (8): subsection (7) prevents the thing done by the body being ended or changed by the body as subsequently constituted`)
-- s 200 (1), (2), (3): the same for the occupant of a position.
#ASSERT `s 200 (1): the function may be exercised by the person for the time being occupying the position` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 200 (1): the function may be exercised by the person for the time being occupying the position` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 200 (2): the thing done by the person ends` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 200 (2): the thing done by the person ends` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`s 200 (3): subsection (2) prevents the thing done by the person being ended or changed by any person subsequently occupying the position`)

§§ `Part 19.5: Service of documents`

-- s 245: applies to a document that is authorised or required under a law to be served, whatever word is used.
#ASSERT `s 245: this part applies to the document` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 245: this part applies to the document` FALSE)

GIVETH A `Facts about a person and the entity`
`a person with no particular role` MEANS
    `Facts about a person and the entity` WITH
        `is concerned with, or takes part in, the management of the corporation or agency` IS FALSE
        `is the director-general of the administrative unit` IS FALSE
        `is the occupant of the position` IS FALSE
        `is entitled, because of the position occupied, to preside at any meeting of the agency at which the person is present` IS FALSE
        `is the chief executive officer (however described) of the agency` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Facts about a person and the entity`
`a person who takes part in management` MEANS
    `Facts about a person and the entity` WITH
        `is concerned with, or takes part in, the management of the corporation or agency` IS TRUE
        `is the director-general of the administrative unit` IS FALSE
        `is the occupant of the position` IS FALSE
        `is entitled, because of the position occupied, to preside at any meeting of the agency at which the person is present` IS FALSE
        `is the chief executive officer (however described) of the agency` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Facts about a person and the entity`
`the director-general` MEANS
    `Facts about a person and the entity` WITH
        `is concerned with, or takes part in, the management of the corporation or agency` IS FALSE
        `is the director-general of the administrative unit` IS TRUE
        `is the occupant of the position` IS FALSE
        `is entitled, because of the position occupied, to preside at any meeting of the agency at which the person is present` IS FALSE
        `is the chief executive officer (however described) of the agency` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Facts about a person and the entity`
`the occupant of the position` MEANS
    `Facts about a person and the entity` WITH
        `is concerned with, or takes part in, the management of the corporation or agency` IS FALSE
        `is the director-general of the administrative unit` IS FALSE
        `is the occupant of the position` IS TRUE
        `is entitled, because of the position occupied, to preside at any meeting of the agency at which the person is present` IS FALSE
        `is the chief executive officer (however described) of the agency` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Facts about a person and the entity`
`the person entitled to preside` MEANS
    `Facts about a person and the entity` WITH
        `is concerned with, or takes part in, the management of the corporation or agency` IS FALSE
        `is the director-general of the administrative unit` IS FALSE
        `is the occupant of the position` IS FALSE
        `is entitled, because of the position occupied, to preside at any meeting of the agency at which the person is present` IS TRUE
        `is the chief executive officer (however described) of the agency` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Facts about a person and the entity`
`the chief executive officer` MEANS
    `Facts about a person and the entity` WITH
        `is concerned with, or takes part in, the management of the corporation or agency` IS FALSE
        `is the director-general of the administrative unit` IS FALSE
        `is the occupant of the position` IS FALSE
        `is entitled, because of the position occupied, to preside at any meeting of the agency at which the person is present` IS FALSE
        `is the chief executive officer (however described) of the agency` IS TRUE

-- s 246, executive officer (a): for a corporation, a person concerned with, or taking part in, the corporation's management.
#ASSERT `s 246: the person is an executive officer of the entity` `a corporation` `a person who takes part in management` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 246: the person is an executive officer of the entity` `a corporation` `a person with no particular role` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 246: the person is an executive officer of the entity` `a corporation` `the director-general` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): for an agency that is an administrative unit, the director-general; and (f) for any agency a person concerned with its management.
#ASSERT `s 246: the person is an executive officer of the entity` `an agency that is an administrative unit` `the director-general` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 246: the person is an executive officer of the entity` `an agency that is an administrative unit` `a person who takes part in management` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 246: the person is an executive officer of the entity` `an agency that is an administrative unit` `a person with no particular role` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c): for an agency that is a statutory office-holder, the occupant of the position.
#ASSERT `s 246: the person is an executive officer of the entity` `an agency that is a statutory office-holder` `the occupant of the position` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 246: the person is an executive officer of the entity` `an agency that is a statutory office-holder` `the director-general` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (d): for an agency constituted by 2 or more people, the person entitled to preside.
#ASSERT `s 246: the person is an executive officer of the entity` `an agency constituted by 2 or more people` `the person entitled to preside` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 246: the person is an executive officer of the entity` `an agency constituted by 2 or more people` `the occupant of the position` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (e): for any other agency, the chief executive officer.
#ASSERT `s 246: the person is an executive officer of the entity` `any other agency` `the chief executive officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 246: the person is an executive officer of the entity` `any other agency` `a person who takes part in management` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 246: the person is an executive officer of the entity` `any other agency` `a person with no particular role` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 246, agency: (a) an administrative unit, (b) a statutory office-holder, (c) any other entity established for a public purpose, and a member of or staff of the agency.
#ASSERT `s 246: the entity is an agency` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 246: the entity is an agency` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 246: the entity is an agency` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 246: the entity is an agency` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 246: the entity is an agency` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 246, corporation does not include an agency.
#ASSERT `s 246: the entity is a corporation for this part` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 246: the entity is a corporation for this part` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 246: the entity is a corporation for this part` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 246, document includes a notice, an article that may be sent by post or anything else.
#ASSERT `s 246: the thing is a document` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 246: the thing is a document` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

GIVEN given IS A BOOLEAN, post IS A BOOLEAN, fax IS A BOOLEAN, email IS A BOOLEAN, left IS A BOOLEAN, age IS A NUMBER, livesOrEmployed IS A BOOLEAN, employed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts about how a document was served`
`the facts of a service` MEANS
    `Facts about how a document was served` WITH
        `it was given to the person to be served, or to an executive officer` IS given
        `it was sent by prepaid post, addressed as the section requires, to an address the section allows` IS post
        `it was faxed to a fax number of the person to be served` IS fax
        `it was emailed to an email address of the person to be served` IS email
        `it was left, addressed as the section requires, at an address the section allows` IS left
        `the apparent age in years of the person it was left with` IS age
        `the person it was left with appears to live or be employed at the address` IS livesOrEmployed
        `the person it was left with appears to be employed at the address` IS employed

-- s 247 (1) (a): by giving it to the individual.
#ASSERT `s 247 (1): the document may be served on an individual in this way` `by giving it to the person, or to an executive officer` (`the facts of a service` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 247 (1): the document may be served on an individual in this way` `by giving it to the person, or to an executive officer` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b): by prepaid post addressed to the individual at a home or business address.
#ASSERT `s 247 (1): the document may be served on an individual in this way` `by sending it by prepaid post` (`the facts of a service` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 247 (1): the document may be served on an individual in this way` `by sending it by prepaid post` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (c): by faxing it to a fax number of the individual. (d): by emailing it to an email address of the individual.
#ASSERT `s 247 (1): the document may be served on an individual in this way` `by fax` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 247 (1): the document may be served on an individual in this way` `by fax` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 247 (1): the document may be served on an individual in this way` `by email` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 247 (1): the document may be served on an individual in this way` `by email` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (e): by leaving it at a home or business address with someone who appears to be at least 16 years old and to live or be employed at the address; both sides of 16.
#ASSERT `s 247 (1): the document may be served on an individual in this way` `by leaving it at an address with someone there` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 16 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 247 (1): the document may be served on an individual in this way` `by leaving it at an address with someone there` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 15 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 247 (1): the document may be served on an individual in this way` `by leaving it at an address with someone there` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 30 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 247 (2): applies to service outside the ACT in the same way.
#ASSERT `s 247 (2): the section applies to the service in the same way as it applies to service in the ACT` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 247 (2): the section applies to the service in the same way as it applies to service in the ACT` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 248 (2): the section applies to the service in the same way as it applies to service in the ACT` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 248 (2): the section applies to the service in the same way as it applies to service in the ACT` FALSE

-- s 248 (1) (a): by giving it to an executive officer of the corporation.
#ASSERT `s 248 (1): the document may be served on a corporation in this way` `by giving it to the person, or to an executive officer` (`the facts of a service` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) post, (c) fax, (d) email.
#ASSERT `s 248 (1): the document may be served on a corporation in this way` `by sending it by prepaid post` (`the facts of a service` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 248 (1): the document may be served on a corporation in this way` `by fax` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 248 (1): the document may be served on a corporation in this way` `by email` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 248 (1): the document may be served on a corporation in this way` `by email` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (e): left with someone who appears to be at least 16 years old and to be employed at the address.
#ASSERT `s 248 (1): the document may be served on a corporation in this way` `by leaving it at an address with someone there` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 16 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 248 (1): the document may be served on a corporation in this way` `by leaving it at an address with someone there` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 15 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 248 (1): the document may be served on a corporation in this way` `by leaving it at an address with someone there` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 40 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 249 (a) to (d): an agency, as for a corporation. (e): left with someone who appears to be employed at the agency (no age).
#ASSERT `s 249: the document may be served on an agency in this way` `by giving it to the person, or to an executive officer` (`the facts of a service` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 249: the document may be served on an agency in this way` `by sending it by prepaid post` (`the facts of a service` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 249: the document may be served on an agency in this way` `by fax` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 249: the document may be served on an agency in this way` `by email` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 249: the document may be served on an agency in this way` `by leaving it at an address with someone there` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 10 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 249: the document may be served on an agency in this way` `by leaving it at an address with someone there` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 40 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 249: the document may be served on an agency in this way` `by leaving it at an address with someone there` (`the facts of a service` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 40 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 250 (2): "subsection (1) does not affect the operation of the Evidence Act 2011, section 160 (Postal articles)".
#ASSERT NOT (`s 250 (2): subsection (1) affects the operation of the Evidence Act 2011, section 160 (Postal articles)`)
-- s 251 (1): "This part does not affect the operation of any other law that authorises or requires service of a document otherwise than as provided under this part."
#ASSERT NOT (`s 251 (1): this part affects the operation of any other law that authorises or requires service of a document otherwise than as provided under this part`)
-- s 251 (2): "Despite this part, a law ... may provide (a) ... only in a particular way ... (b) for the date (or date and time) when service ... is taken to have been made."
#ASSERT `s 251 (2) (a): a law may provide that a document of a particular kind may or must be served only in a particular way or to a particular address or number`
#ASSERT `s 251 (2) (b): a law may provide for the date, or date and time, when service of a document is taken to have been made`
-- s 252: "This part does not affect the power of a court or tribunal to authorise or require service of a document otherwise than as provided under this part."
#ASSERT NOT (`s 252: this part affects the power of a court or tribunal to authorise or require service of a document otherwise than as provided under this part`)
